<title>ROMANIA: Romania Sanevit sees higher 1996 profit.</title>
<headline>Romania Sanevit sees higher 1996 profit.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million of leu unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit			   1,186    vs     433.717</p>
<p> Turnover			    10,378    vs   1,532</p>
<p> Fixed assets			48,498    vs  30,975</p>
<p> Working capital		    6,108    vs   4,841</p>
<p> Total assets			59.565    vs  44.956</p>
<p> Share capital		     24.657    vs  24.657</p>
<p> Total debts			 24.288    vs   8.926</p>
<p> Total dividends		    1,095</p>
<p>NOTE -- Sanevit, a private company listed on the Bucharest stock exchange, is Romania's sole disposable syringe maker. Data reported are in nominal terms and according to Romanian accounting standards.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
